# Project Workflow

- Start with `README.md` to find the right docs for the task.
- Before implementation, read `planning.md` and any relevant docs under `docs/`.
- Treat `docs/log-catalog.md` as the source of truth for log items.
- Treat `docs/rule-catalog.md` as the source of truth for reminders, feedback, and warning rules.
- Follow a docs-first workflow: update canonical docs before changing schema, types, UI, or logic.
- If code and docs disagree, align the docs first, then update the code.
- Keep business logic out of page components when possible.
- Add short `###` comments only for non-obvious intent, assumptions, or tricky behavior.
